  "id": "COMPOUND:38316 - PROTEIN:4911",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between 2,4,6-Trimethylhepta-1,3,6-triene and CD276 antigen through a series of target interactions involving members of the Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family. This compound is identified as a target of multiple compounds, including (2E,4E)-N-isobutylundeca-2,4-dien-8,10-diynamide, Phorone, and Ajugaciliatin E, all of which are themselves targets of CD276 antigen. The shared target of these compounds points to a potential mechanism where 2,4,6-Trimethylhepta-1,3,6-triene may influence CD276 antigen through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of the SDR family members. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional link between the compound and CD276 antigen. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of the SDR family in mediating interactions with CD276 antigen, suggesting a broader role in drug-target relationships.",
